                    {
                        "name":  "places/ChIJI0ufUFirQjQRz254cAjj26M/reviews/ChZDSUhNMG9nS0VJQ0FnSUNydkotV0lnEAE",
                        "relativePublishTimeDescription":  "a year ago",
                        "rating":  5,
                        "text":  {
                                     "text":  "I didn’t make a reservation but luckily the host gave me a seat at the bar beside the door for me and my dining companion. Normally I’d be very unhappy with this seat since it is directly beside the door and the air conditioner pipe drips condensation, but the host was really amazing and wiped it for us making our experience much better. The interior of the restaurant is long and narrow with all wood finishing and furnishings giving you the Japanese bbq vibe you’re looking for. The food is delicious and we got an assortment of skewers which were all very well cooked. They had a few varieties of sake and beer all of which did their job perfectly. The true star of the show though, was the salmon fried rice which was a real surprisingly delightful dish that both I and my friend enjoyed thoroughly. Also this place is open pretty late so if you’re looking for some good eats after hours, then you got to give this place a try.",
                                     "languageCode":  "en"
                                 },
                        "originalText":  {
